      "writtenOn": "2024-06-28T08:19:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I checked that the \"min-level\" feature is already supported in the vintf parser [1], and the logic for filtering HALs based on the device manifest level is present in [VintfObject::filterHalsByDeviceManifestLevel](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/libvintf/VintfObject.cpp;l\u003d528;drc\u003dd5137445c0d4067406cb3e38aade5507ff2fcd16).\n\nOtherwise, I have flashed the device with images both before and after this change, and the AVF RKP HAL is successfully removed as expected.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/search?ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain\u0026q\u003df:vintf%20min-level",
      "parentUuid": "a8d2f4b5_75a74680",
      "revId": "1abde134ba6564d9d0633549d2c0aa7c9896e6c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
